==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|knotty}}, {{m|enm|knotti}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|knot|y}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-knotty.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|naughty}} {{qualifier|in accents with the [[w:cot-caught merger|cot-caught merger]]}}
:* {{rhymes|ɒti|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# Full of [[knot]]s.
#: '''''knotty''' pine''
# [[complicated|Complicated]] or [[tricky]]; [[complex]]; [[difficult]].
#: ''a '''knotty''' problem''

